precheck.shell.lic.node	0
precheck.shell.lic.pnpm	0
precheck.shell.lic.mise	0
precheck.shell.ic.claude	0
precheck.shell.ic.codex	0
precheck.shell.ic.gh	0
precheck.shell.ic.git	0
precheck.shell.ic.node	0
precheck.shell.ic.pnpm	0
precheck.shell.ic.mise	0
precheck.shell.lc.claude	0
precheck.shell.lc.codex	0
precheck.shell.lc.gh	0
precheck.shell.lc.git	0
precheck.shell.lc.node	0
precheck.shell.lc.pnpm	0
precheck.shell.lc.mise	0
os	linux
env.root	0
env.login_shell	bash
env.pkg.apt	1
env.pkg.dnf	0
env.pkg.pacman	0
env.pkg.zypper	0
env.userns.restricted	apparmor
transcript.exit	0
transcript.verdict	clean
transcript.warn_count	0
info.0001	Installing mise (a version manager for your tools)...
info.0002	Not a terminal — skipping gh auth. Run 'gh auth login' later.
info.0003	Installing git (your system will ask for your password)...
info.0004	Your computer wants the password you use to log in. Nothing appears as you type - that is normal. Press Return when you're done.
info.0005	Not signed into GitHub yet — sign in (gh auth login), then re-run to set your git name/email.
info.0006	Your agent instructions live in one file:
info.0007	Both Claude and Codex read it (linked from their own config).
info.0008	💡 Edit that file in plain language to steer every future session.
info.0009	Claude config already exists — leaving it; you may see a one-time trust prompt.
info.0010	Your first message to the agent is saved here:
info.0011	Run 'claude' in $HOME/git/first-project to start (you'll sign in on first launch).
info.0012	A starter message is saved in $HOME/git/first-project/first-message.txt — paste it in as your first message.
